---
/**
 * Indoors — museums, science centers and libraries.
 *
 * The section exists because of the weather, not because of the institutions.
 * Nobody wakes up wanting a county historical society; they wake up to rain
 * with a rental house and two kids in it. So the page is organized around
 * "what's open today and does it cost anything", and the H1 says the weather
 * part out loud.
 *
 * Hours lead every card. A park is open; these are shut four days a week or
 * shut all winter, and the failure mode is a locked door at the end of a
 * forty-minute drive.
 */
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import FlagIcon from "../../components/FlagIcon.astro";
import CardPhoto from "../../components/CardPhoto.astro";
import Tag from "../../components/Tag.astro";

import indoorData from "../../data/indoor.json";
import { completeness, hoursAnswer, present, type IndoorPlace } from "../../lib/indoor";
import { isPublishable, robotsFor } from "../../lib/verification";
import { byPhotoThen } from "../../lib/order";

const places = indoorData as unknown as IndoorPlace[];
const live = places.filter(isPublishable);
const gate = {
  verifiedDate: null,
  verifiedSource: null,
  sources: live.length ? [{ label: "x", url: "x" }] : null,
  sourcedOn: live.length ? "2026-08-04" : null,
};

const free = places.filter((p) => p.admission.free === true).length;
const unknownAdmission = places.filter((p) => p.admission.free === null).length;
const seasonal = places.filter((p) => p.hours.season !== null).length;

const ranked = byPhotoThen(places, (a, b) => completeness(b).known - completeness(a).known);
---

<Layout
  title="Deep Creek museums and libraries — hours and admission"
  description="Museums, the Discovery Center and all five library branches around Deep Creek Lake: opening hours, what admission costs, what's inside. Where to go when it rains."
  robots={robotsFor(gate)}
>
  <div class="wrap pt-11 pb-6">
    <p class="label m-0">Indoors</p>
    <h1 class="text-[2.2rem] sm:text-[2.9rem] mt-3.5 mb-0 max-w-[15ch] text-slate">
      When it rains
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-5 mb-0 text-[1.15rem] leading-[1.5] max-w-[54ch]">
      Museums, the Discovery Center and the county library. Everywhere here is
      warm, dry and indoors. The rest of the site covers
      <a href="/parks/">the days you can get outside</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap prose-field pb-2">
    <h2>Check the hours before you drive</h2>
    <p class="max-w-[58ch]">
      This is the one part of the county where turning up unannounced doesn't
      work. Most of these open four days a week. One shuts from October to May.
      The Discovery Center doesn't publish hours at all, just a phone number.
    </p>

    <p class="max-w-[58ch]">
      So hours sit at the top of every card and every page here, and where I
      don't know them it says so instead of implying you're welcome.
    </p>

    <div class="sheet breakout my-6 px-4 sm:px-5 py-4">
      <p class="label m-0">Where this dataset stands</p>
      <dl class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-4 mt-3 mb-0">
        {
          [
            { n: places.length, label: "places listed" },
            { n: free, label: "confirmed free" },
            { n: unknownAdmission, label: "price unknown" },
            { n: seasonal, label: "close for a season" },
          ].map((s) => (
            <div>
              <dt class="font-display text-[2rem] font-semibold text-slate leading-none">{s.n}</dt>
              <dd class="m-0 mt-1 stamp text-ink-soft">{s.label}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
      <p class="mt-3.5 mb-0 text-[0.9rem] leading-snug text-ink-soft max-w-[56ch]">
        Three of these publish hours on their own site but no admission price at
        all. That's not an oversight on my end — it's genuinely not published,
        and the calls are on the list.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap pb-8">
    <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 breakout">
      {
        ranked.map((place) => {
          const { known, total } = completeness(place);
          const hrs = hoursAnswer(place.hours);
          const has = present(place);
          return (
            <article data-reveal class="sheet sheet-action relative group overflow-hidden">
              <a href={`/indoors/${place.slug}/`} class="absolute inset-0 z-10 no-underline">
                <span class="sr-only">{place.name}</span>
              </a>

              {place.photos?.[0] && <CardPhoto {...place.photos[0]} />}

              <div class="p-4 sm:p-5">
                <header class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
                  <div>
                    <h2 class="font-display text-[1.12rem] font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] m-0 text-slate underline decoration-contour decoration-2 underline-offset-[0.16em] group-hover:decoration-slate">
                      {place.name}
                    </h2>
                    <p class="stamp text-ink-soft mt-1 mb-0">{place.kind} · {place.town}</p>
                  </div>
                  <span class="stamp text-ink-soft shrink-0">{known}/{total}</span>
                </header>

                {/* Hours first, always, and visually separated. */}
                <div class="mt-3.5 border-y-2 border-contour py-2.5">
                  <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3">
                    <span class="label">Open</span>
                    <span
                      class={`text-[0.9rem] text-right leading-snug ${
                        hrs.state === "unknown" ? "text-ink-soft italic" : "text-ink font-medium"
                      }`}
                    >
                      {hrs.text}
                    </span>
                  </div>
                  {place.hours.season && (
                    <p class="stamp text-flag-red-bearing mt-1.5 mb-0 text-right">{place.hours.season}</p>
                  )}
                </div>

                <p class="mt-3 mb-0 text-[0.9rem] leading-[1.55]">{place.blurb}</p>

                {has.length > 0 && (
                  <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 mt-3.5 flex flex-wrap gap-1.5">
                    {has.map((f) => (
                      <Tag icon={f.key as any} label={f.label} emphasis={f.emphasis} />
                    ))}
                  </ul>
                )}

                {place.warnings.length > 0 && (
                  <p class="mt-3 mb-0 text-[0.85rem] leading-snug text-ink-soft flex gap-1.5">
                    <FlagIcon icon="alert" class="w-[1em] h-[1em] mt-1 shrink-0 text-flag-red" />
                    <span>{place.warnings[0]}</span>
                  </p>
                )}

                <p class="stamp text-ink-soft mt-3.5 mb-0 flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
                  <span>{place.operator}</span>
                  <span class="text-contour-deep group-hover:translate-x-0.5 transition-transform duration-100">→</span>
                </p>
              </div>
            </article>
          );
        })
      }
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap prose-field pb-4">
    <h2>Why a library is in here</h2>
    <p class="max-w-[58ch]">
      Because on a wet Tuesday it's the most reliable indoor room in the county.
      Free, warm, has a bathroom, and nobody minds how long you stay. The five
      branches all keep different hours, which is exactly the kind of thing
      that's a nuisance to look up five times, so they're in one table.
    </p>

    <h2>Related</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/parks/">The state parks and forests</a></li>
      <li><a href="/parks/regional/">Town parks</a></li>
      <li><a href="/events/">Fairs and events</a></li>
      <li><a href="/verified/">Every fact on the site, with its source</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Layout>
